   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law and the public authorities law, in\nrelation to notice procedures prior to approval of projects by industrial\ndevelopment agencies",
    "basePrintNo": "S1337",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1337-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 32,
       "fullName": "Luis R. Sepúlveda",
       "imgName": "493_Luis_Sepulveda.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1142,
       "sessionMemberId": 2034,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "SEPULVEDA"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§859-a & 874, Gen Muni L; amd §§1953-a, 1963-a, 2307 & 2315, Pub Auth L (as proposed in S.3256 & A.10056)",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S1337\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law and the public authorities\nlaw, in relation to notice procedures prior to approval of projects by\nindustrial development agencies\n\n \nPURPOSE OF BILL:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of L.2022,\nc.766.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by permitting notices via\nemail.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe underlying legislation required Industrial Development Agencies\n(IDAs) to send notifications of proposed financial incentives for a\nproject and any reasons for deviation from their uniform tax exemption\npolicy to affected local taxing jurisdictions by certified mail, return\nreceipt requested.\n\nPursuant to approval memo 68 of 2022, the Executive and Legislature\nreached this agreement to allow notices required by the underlying chap-\nter to occur by email with a read-receipt (as opposed to only be certi-\nfied mail), and to require IDAs to establish procedures for complying\nwith the notification requirement and identifying the notification meth-\nod that will be used for local taxing jurisdictions.  In cases of school\ndistrict notifications, the chapter amendment changes the entity who\nwill he notified from the school board to the district clerk, as the\ndistrict clerk is the usual and customary recipient of notices to school\ndistricts.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 766 of the Laws of 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the General Municipal Law and the\nPublic Authorities Law relating to requiring notice and confirmation of\nsuch notice by affected local taxing jurisdictions and school districts\nprior to approval of projects by industrial development agencies, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S.  3256 and A. 10056, takes\neffect.\n",
